        "id": 1809421
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-06T05:55:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this is not valid across sessions, then why have bytes at all? This could just be a Key AIDL object. (incidentally this would clean up the `IHwCryptoKeyProperties` interface as the key could just have its own interface, and we could probably simplify a lot of the other interfaces by putting methods on the Key). I kind of like the idea of a key being a first-class AIDL object. If you need a wrapped representation that can later be re-imported, then you can have a method that returns these bytes.",
      "parentUuid": "49615582_5094c6e5",
      "revId": "596f627b3a10f7c853acfb165da1a6ccdd0c089b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
