      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-08T00:13:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea is that the service implementer can use those bytes to outsource storing keys to the client side. I am not sure how important that is, but is a pattern I\u0027ve seen on KM and on an additional crypto related spec I\u0027ve been reviewing. Making the key an AIDL object would mean to change it from a `parcelable` to an `interface` and keep any needed information just on the server side?",
